  "result": "I wrote your 10-minute lesson on context and memory (objective O3). It's at `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html`.\n\nThe lesson covers three concepts, each starting from a makerspace example:\n1. **The context window.** The program re-sends everything to the model at every step, so the context grows and costs tokens each time. The example is a laser-cutter booking.\n2. **Notes between sessions.** Facts that must outlast a session, like a student's training status, have to be written to storage and loaded back later.\n3. **Just-in-time retrieval.** The assistant searches a 300-page manual and pulls in only the page it needs.\n\nIt also has a warm-up on the agent loop, three practice questions with instant feedback, a worked example, a \"your turn\" exercise and a summary.\n\nI only read the Anthropic context-engineering post in full. The context-window docs page is linked from search results but I didn't open it. Both are recorded in `RESOURCES.md`. I found no community to link yet.\n\nI did not read `learning-records/` before writing, and I did not count the words. I planned about 1,500 and expect it to land near that. I left compaction (summarizing a long conversation) for a later lesson.\n\nI added a line to `NOTES.md` about this lesson. Quiz 0001 (the agent loop) is still ungraded.\n\nYou can ask me for a quiz on this lesson whenever you're ready, or ask me anything about it.",
